Installation Instructions for Hyper Math
========================================

Copyright (C) 2026 Kival

Basic Installation
------------------

Hyper Math adheres to the GNU Coding Standards and can be built and installed
using either GNU Make directly or CMake.

1. Building with GNU Make (Recommended):

     make
     make check
     make install PREFIX=/usr/local

   Standard GNU Make directory variables are honored:
     - `prefix`      (default: `/usr/local`)
     - `exec_prefix` (default: `$(prefix)`)
     - `bindir`      (default: `$(exec_prefix)/bin`)
     - `libdir`      (default: `$(exec_prefix)/lib`)
     - `includedir`  (default: `$(prefix)/include`)
     - `DESTDIR`     (staging root directory for packaged installs)

2. Building with CMake:

     mkdir -p build && cd build
     cmake .. -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
     cmake --build .
     ctest --output-on-failure
     cmake --install . --prefix /usr/local

Compiler Requirements
---------------------

Hyper Math requires a C++20 compliant compiler (such as GCC >= 11 or Clang >= 14)
and relies on zero external third-party libraries.
